<title>THAILAND: Tuntex Plc to take $170 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Tuntex Plc to take $170 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tuntex (Thailand) Plc said on Monday it would borrow $170 million from Bangkok Bank Plc to buy machinery to boost its polymer production.</p>
<p>The eight-year loan would be taken in early May at an interest rate of LIBOR plus 2.5 percent.</p>
<p>The planned machinery purchase would enable the company to more than double its polymer production to 660 tonnes per day from the current 300 tones per day, it said in a filing to the Thai stock exchange. No further details were given.</p>
</text>
